-- title:
--   Complete Part Proj Family Self Consistency Generic
-- statement:
--   **Complete-part projection families inherit self consistency from the slice family.**
--
--   Let `psi_bi` be a bipartite state and assume the family satisfies the complete G self-consistency statement at level `zeta`. Then the one-outcome complete-part projection family has the corresponding switcheroo self-consistency relation over the uniform slice-question distribution:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDRel}\!\left(\psi_{bi},\mathcal D_{\mathrm{slice}},
--   \mathrm{switcherooSelfConsistencyLeft},
--   \mathrm{switcherooSelfConsistencyRight},\zeta\right).
--   $$
--
--   The result converts the original slice-family hypothesis into the exact relation required by the second aggregate-term comparison and the complete-part commuting-with-G argument.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.completePartProjFamily_selfConsistency_generic`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/SwitcherooCompletion/SecondTerm.lean#L22-L56

